Chapter: Arm64VirtioBlkProbe
  cites Kernel chapter Arm64Pci
  cites Kernel chapter VirtioPci
  cites Kernel chapter VirtioBlk
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 Phase 4 of OracleCloudArm64.md was "unmeasured, not passing": nothing in
 any boot payload ever called VirtioBlk. This calls it.

 It doubles as the control the virtio-net investigation lacks. VirtioBlk
 rides the SAME VirtioPci transport as VirtioNet but is a different device
 with one queue, and the disk it talks to is the one the firmware just
 booted this image from, so the device is known good. If the read
 succeeds, the transport works and the TX fault is net-specific. If it
 fails the same way -- notify issued, used ring never advances -- the
 fault is in the shared transport and VirtioNet is only where it was
 noticed.

 The oracle is the content of sector 0, not a pointer test: byte 510 is
 0x55 and byte 511 is 0xAA in any protective MBR, and byte 450 is 0xEE,
 the GPT protective partition type. A read that returns 512 zero bytes
 passes a "did we get a buffer" test and fails this one.

Section: Device Discovery

  bp-find-blk : Arm64PciScanResult -> Arm64PciDevice
  bp-find-blk (scan) =
   when arm64-pci-find-device scan #1AF4 #1042
    is Just (d) -> d
    is None -> when arm64-pci-find-device scan #1AF4 #1001
      is Just (d2) -> d2
      is None -> list-at (scan.devices) 0

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Integer = act
    print-line-uni "arm64-virtio-blk-probe"
    let scan = arm64-pci-scan-bus 0
    in let dev = bp-find-blk scan
    in let enabled = arm64-pci-enable-device dev
    in act
      print-line-uni ("pci count=" & show (scan.count)
        & " vendor=" & show (dev.pci-vendor)
        & " device=" & show (dev.pci-device-id))
      let st = virtio-blk-init dev
      in act
        print-line-uni ("capacity=" & show (st.capacity)
          & " sectors, queue-size=" & show ((st.queue).queue-size)
          & " notify-addr=" & show ((st.queue).notify-addr))
        let r = virtio-blk-read-sector st 0
        in let d = r.data
        in act
          (print-line-uni ("read ok=" & show (r.ok)
            & " len=" & show (list-length d)
            & " b450=" & show (list-at d 450)
            & " b510=" & show (list-at d 510)
            & " b511=" & show (list-at d 511)
            & " want 238 85 170"))
          0
        end
      end
    end
  end

